      "description": "Watch Deportivo Riestra vs Barracas Central highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 2, 2026. On August 2, 2026, Deportivo Riestra hosted Barracas Central in a highly anticipated Liga Profesional Argentina encounter. Both sides entered the pitch looking to assert their dominance in a fixture that promised plenty of tactical intrigue and physical competition. Grit and Discipline in the Opening Period The first half was characterized by a gritty, defensive struggle as both teams looked to find their rhythm. The referee was kept busy as the intensity of the midfield battle increased, leading to several early bookings. Nicolas Watson was the first to enter the book in the 21st minute, followed shortly after by Facundo Bruera in the 31st minute. Deportivo Riestra attempted to push forward, but they found it difficult to break down a well-organized Barracas Central defensive line that remained disciplined throughout the first 45 minutes. Maroni Breaks the Deadlock The second half saw a shift in momentum as both managers turned to their benches to find a spark. The breakthrough finally arrived in the 72nd minute when Tomas Porra delivered a sublime assist into the path of Gonzalo Maroni . The midfielder showed great composure to clinicaly finish the chance and put Barracas Central ahead. Following the goal, Deportivo Riestra introduced Brian Sanchez and Pablo Monje in an attempt to claw their way back into the game, but the visitors remained resilient under pressure. Late Drama and the Final Whistle As the clock ticked toward full-time, the tension reached a boiling point. Gonzalo Maroni , who had earlier been the hero, received a yellow card in stoppage time for a tactical foul as Barracas Central fought to protect their lead. Despite late tactical adjustments from both sides, including the introduction of Juan Barbieri for the hosts, Deportivo Riestra could not find the equalizer. The final whistle confirmed a hard-fought away victory for Barracas Central , secured by that solitary clinical strike from Maroni."
